block_dim justification (A2-K1, 910B3)

Shipped block_dim = 40. It is NOT assumed: the dual-oracle acceptance
(tests/test_a2_gdn_chunk.py, numbers in acceptance_numbers.log) runs at bd=40 and
matches both CPU fp32 oracles (block-solve + grouped-recurrent) to ~3e-7 across all
ABI gaps + segment chaining, and the backward matches autograd to ~1.6e-7-5.2e-7.
At bd=40 the B*HV work is one item per cube core (per=CeilDiv(B*HV, GetCubeNum())),
so there is no cross-core L0C sharing and no M10-081 race surface; a race would show
as a wrong result against the oracle, and none does.

A bd=1 cross-check was attempted (one build per process) but bd=1 FAULTS on device
(vector core exception) — a single-core work-partition path that is not the shipped
configuration. So bd=40 is pinned as the single verified value in contract.json,
matching how the other a2 units pin only verified block_dim values (they could not
verify large bd; here bd=40 is the verified+shipped one). bd portability beyond 40 is
untested and not claimed.
